From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] host breakpoints for KVM and WHPX: guest fixups under WHPX

The pvg guest fixups patch Tahoe's Metal code right before it runs, from
an instruction breakpoint owned by host code; that was KVM only
(kvm_set_host_breakpoints, kvm_walk_user_pages). Now behind an
accelerator-neutral API, system/host-breakpoints.h:

- host_set_breakpoints(): KVM as before; WHPX loads the addresses into the
  guest's DR0..DR3/DR7 on each vCPU's next entry and intercepts #DB while
  any are set (all vCPUs paused to change that partition property). A hit
  runs the callback with the BQL and resumes with RF set; other #DBs are
  injected back as before.
- the debug registers are guest-visible under WHPX, so the fixups re-arm
  them every 2 s (host_breakpoints_need_rearm()).
- guest_walk_user_pages(): the x86 page walk, moved out of kvm.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
